    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "The Lord Challenges Job"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Then the Lord answered Job from the whirlwind:"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“Who is this that questions my wisdom",
          "with such ignorant words?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Brace yourself like a man,",
          "because I have some questions for you,",
          "and you must answer them."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“Where were you when I laid the foundations of the earth?",
          "Tell me, if you know so much."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Who determined its dimensions",
          "and stretched out the surveying line?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "What supports its foundations,",
          "and who laid its cornerstone"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "as the morning stars sang together",
          "and all the angels shouted for joy?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“Who kept the sea inside its boundaries",
          "as it burst from the womb,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "and as I clothed it with clouds",
          "and wrapped it in thick darkness?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For I locked it behind barred gates,",
          "limiting its shores."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I said, ‘This far and no farther will you come.",
          "Here your proud waves must stop!’"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“Have you ever commanded the morning to appear",
          "and caused the dawn to rise in the east?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Have you made daylight spread to the ends of the earth,",
          "to bring an end to the night’s wickedness?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          14
        ],
        "lines": [
          "As the light approaches,",
          "the earth takes shape like clay pressed beneath a seal;",
          "it is robed in brilliant colors."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          15
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The light disturbs the wicked",
          "and stops the arm that is raised in violence."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          16
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“Have you explored the springs from which the seas come?",
          "Have you explored their depths?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          17
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Do you know where the gates of death are located?",
          "Have you seen the gates of utter gloom?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          18
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Do you realize the extent of the earth?",
          "Tell me about it if you know!"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          19
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“Where does light come from,",
          "and where does darkness go?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          20
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Can you take each to its home?",
          "Do you know how to get there?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          21
        ],
        "lines": [
          "But of course you know all this!",
          "For you were born before it was all created,",
          "and you are so very experienced!"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          22
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“Have you visited the storehouses of the snow",
          "or seen the storehouses of hail?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          23
        ],
        "lines": [
          "(I have reserved them as weapons for the time of trouble,",
          "for the day of battle and war.)"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          24
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Where is the path to the source of light?",
          "Where is the home of the east wind?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          25
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“Who created a channel for the torrents of rain?",
          "Who laid out the path for the lightning?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          26
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Who makes the rain fall on barren land,",
          "in a desert where no one lives?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          27
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Who sends rain to satisfy the parched ground",
          "and make the tender grass spring up?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          28
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“Does the rain have a father?",
          "Who gives birth to the dew?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          29
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Who is the mother of the ice?",
          "Who gives birth to the frost from the heavens?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          30
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For the water turns to ice as hard as rock,",
          "and the surface of the water freezes."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          31
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“Can you direct the movement of the stars—",
          "binding the cluster of the Pleiades",
          "or loosening the cords of Orion?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          32
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Can you direct the constellations through the seasons",
          "or guide the Bear with her cubs across the heavens?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          33
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Do you know the laws of the universe?",
          "Can you use them to regulate the earth?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          34
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“Can you shout to the clouds",
          "and make it rain?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          35
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Can you make lightning appear",
          "and cause it to strike as you direct?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          36
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Who gives intuition to the heart",
          "and instinct to the mind?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          37
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Who is wise enough to count all the clouds?",
          "Who can tilt the water jars of heaven"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          38
        ],
        "lines": [
          "when the parched ground is dry",
          "and the soil has hardened into clods?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          39
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“Can you stalk prey for a lioness",
          "and satisfy the young lions’ appetites"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          40
        ],
        "lines": [
          "as they lie in their dens",
          "or crouch in the thicket?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          41
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Who provides food for the ravens",
          "when their young cry out to God",
          "and wander about in hunger?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      }
    ]
  },
